$Module wasm 3 "Wasm VMOD"

$Synopsis manual

$Event vmod_event

DESCRIPTION
===========

Embeds a WebAssembly runtime (Wasmtime) into Varnish for
request/response filtering via Proxy-Wasm ABI v0.2.1.

$Function VOID load(STRING name, STRING path)

$Restrict vcl_init

Load and compile a .wasm module. Example::

    wasm.load("filter", "/etc/varnish/wasm/filter.wasm");

$Function INT execute(STRING name, STRING function)

$Restrict client

Call an exported function (non-proxy-wasm path). Returns i32 result. Example::

    if (wasm.execute("mod", "check") == 403) { return (synth(403)); }

$Function STRING version()

Return the vmod-wasm version string.

$Function VOID set_fuel(INT fuel)

$Restrict vcl_init

Max instruction fuel per execution. Default 1000000. Example::

    wasm.set_fuel(500000);

$Function VOID set_memory_limit(INT limit)

$Restrict vcl_init

Max Wasm linear memory in bytes. Default 16 MiB. Example::

    wasm.set_memory_limit(8388608);

$Function INT get_fuel()

Return the current fuel limit.

$Function INT get_memory_limit()

Return the current memory limit in bytes.

$Function INT proxy_wasm_on_request(STRING module)

$Restrict client

Run Proxy-Wasm request lifecycle. Returns 0 (continue), >0 (local response status), or -1 (error). Example::

    set req.http.X-Wasm = wasm.proxy_wasm_on_request("filter");

$Function INT proxy_wasm_on_response(STRING module)

$Restrict vcl_backend_response vcl_deliver

Run Proxy-Wasm response lifecycle. Same return semantics. Example::

    set resp.http.X-Wasm = wasm.proxy_wasm_on_response("filter");

$Function INT proxy_wasm_on_request_configured(STRING module, STRING vm_config, STRING plugin_config)

$Restrict client

Like proxy_wasm_on_request but passes vm_config/plugin_config to the module. Example::

    set req.http.X-Wasm = wasm.proxy_wasm_on_request_configured(
        "filter", "{}", "{\"block\": \"/admin\"}");

$Function INT proxy_wasm_on_response_configured(STRING module, STRING vm_config, STRING plugin_config)

$Restrict vcl_backend_response vcl_deliver

Like proxy_wasm_on_response but passes vm_config/plugin_config to the module. Example::

    set resp.http.X-Wasm = wasm.proxy_wasm_on_response_configured(
        "filter", "", "{\"add_header\": \"X-Filtered\"}");

$Function VOID set_allowed_upstreams(STRING upstream_list)

$Restrict vcl_init

Comma-separated "host:port" allowlist for proxy_http_call (SSRF prevention). Example::

    wasm.set_allowed_upstreams("api.internal:8080,auth.svc:443");

$Function VOID set_http_call_limit(INT limit)

$Restrict vcl_init

Max HTTP callouts per request. Default 5, 0 disables. Example::

    wasm.set_http_call_limit(3);

$Function VOID set_fail_mode(STRING mode)

$Restrict vcl_init

"closed" (default): errors return -1. "open": errors return 0. Example::

    wasm.set_fail_mode("open");

$Function STRING get_stats_json()

Return execution statistics as JSON. Counters are atomic and thread-safe. Example::

    set resp.http.X-Wasm-Stats = wasm.get_stats_json();

$Function STRING get_metrics_json()

Return Proxy-Wasm metrics as JSON. Returns "{}" if empty. Example::

    synthetic(wasm.get_metrics_json());
